# The trigger needs noncombat damage dealt to an opponent (CR 120.2, 510.2): Bot1's Memnite deals 1 combat damage to Bot2 (turn 3),
# a Lightning Bolt kills Bot2's Ornithopter (damage to a creature), and a second Bolt hits Bot1 itself (turn 5). Each would be asked
# "exile that many cards?" if it triggered; none is, so nothing is exiled and the script's next lines are not displaced by a question.

[Bot1 Deck]
Mox Ruby
Mox Jet
Mox Pearl
Mox Sapphire
Mountain
Virtue of Courage
Memnite
Lightning Bolt
Lightning Bolt
Mountain x12

[Bot2 Deck]
Ornithopter
Island x19

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Mox Ruby.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Jet.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Pearl.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Sapphire.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mountain.Play
Bot1.Hand.Memnite.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Virtue of Courage.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Ruby.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mountain.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Jet.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Pearl.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Sapphire.Activate
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
[T2 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Ornithopter.Cast
[T3 Bot1.DeclareAttackers]
Bot1.Attack(Memnite > Bot2)
Bot2.Block(Count: 0)
[T3 Bot1.Main2]
? Bot2.Life = 19
? Exile.Count = 0
Bot1.Hand.Lightning Bolt.Cast(Bot2.Battlefield.Ornithopter)
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Ruby.Activate
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
? Bot2.Graveyard = Ornithopter
? Exile.Count = 0
[T5 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Hand.Lightning Bolt.Cast(Bot1)
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Ruby.Activate
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass

[Expect]
Bot1.Life = 17
Bot2.Life = 19
Exile.Count = 0
Bot1.Graveyard = Lightning Bolt; Lightning Bolt
